{"title":"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(duality_principle)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (duality principle)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Trigonometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Trigonometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Ravi_Substitution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Ravi Substitution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the lengths of a triangle whose area is <i>S</i>.  Prove that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/f/fef898558ae7541eb052941b83d871b393e690ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2 + c^2 \\ge 4S\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"162\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>In what case does equality hold?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By Heron's formula, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/a/29aaa9ecf6a0a74c3caa5e12547b5e517274b5c8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S = \\sqrt{s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)}.\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"32\" />\nThis can be simplified to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d9fcb4ae64a2bc2dd021e1cbc537b73b0d26a29.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S = \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{a+b+c}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{-a+b+c}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{a-b+c}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{a+b-c}{2}\\right)}.\\]\" width=\"480\" height=\"53\" />\nNext, we can factor out all of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s and use a clever difference of squares:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/3/5f308d32f84fa188ad0f9b597b1413f28ae58912.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S = \\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{(a+b+c)(-a+b+c)(a-b+c)(a+b-c)}\\]\" width=\"417\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39fc029f2475de0695efa2ffa8e59645501a1c32.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S = \\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{((b+c)^2 - a^2)(a^2 - (b-c)^2)}\\]\" width=\"292\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/f/59fc0cae65677eee7ff76e8a4cf9dd024bb4238b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S = \\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{(2bc + b^2 + c^2 - a^2)(2bc - b^2 - c^2 + a^2)}.\\]\" width=\"376\" height=\"37\" />\nWe can now use difference of squares again:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/c/9bc382e4a4f186baf19cf7eab4248ea1ed1d3e3c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S = \\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{4b^2c^2-(b^2 + c^2 - a^2)^2}\\]\" width=\"243\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbbb8a638ff4c36e07930cf1d07e942f123ec1cd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4S\\sqrt{3} = \\sqrt{3(4b^2c^2 - (b^2 + c^2 - a^2)^2)}\\]\" width=\"286\" height=\"32\" />\nWe must prove that the RHS of this equation is less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/e/67ef60c31efe92506e822825c1faf350b5d08714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2 + c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/9/bf9d29e6148a598345dc0c9a5c301cbed0d66a70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 = A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/1/d016210095051d51c2a7a6bb363032cc90e8575a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2 = B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f48bfaedad3f183e51dc0bdb9578c85e97bc12c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^2 = C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"17\" />. Then, our inequality can be reduced to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/b/aeba0d284827b200acad9d1cc527390509d0481a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A + B + C \\geq \\sqrt{6AB + 6BC + 6CA - 3A^2 - 3B^2 - 3C^2}.\\]\" width=\"445\" height=\"19\" />\nWe now have to prove\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/5/745a28c72fe76e9d4c060dd600cdce8997ff004a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(A + B + C)^2 \\geq 6AB + 6BC + 6CA - 3A^2 - 3B^2 - 3C^2.\\]\" width=\"451\" height=\"20\" />\nWe can simplify:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/2/c62e742e7c9d6d1ac4d5bf4a607914d63a58ff1e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A^2 + B^2 + C^2 + 2AB + 2BC + 2CA \\geq 6AB + 6BC + 6CA - 3A^2 - 3B^2 - 3C^2\\]\" width=\"546\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/e/7dea19eae08abc2763ff2d067970644d83d8b03a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4A^2 + 4B^2 + 4C^2 \\geq 4AB + 4BC + 4CA\\]\" width=\"317\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/b/6db0f38840293c70ab8077e5f9040a13eaf1544c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A^2 + B^2 + C^2 \\geq AB + BC + CA.\\]\" width=\"266\" height=\"18\" />\nFinally, we can apply AM-GM:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/9/6f9872670475347077707b895b6f8f900a3c8b10.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{A^2 + B^2}{2} \\geq AB\\]\" width=\"119\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/3/8e36040e650e789c980336743f7799f7010a4b30.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{B^2 + C^2}{2} \\geq BC\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc9747c3e015150bf8d6eba584e0b58268233b46.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{C^2 + A^2}{2} \\geq CA\\]\" width=\"119\" height=\"39\" />\nAdding these all up, we have the desired inequality\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/9/b59c28bac016f6b88cefb3de1fbe20911ceeae83.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A^2 + B^2 + C^2 \\geq AB + BC + CA,\\]\" width=\"267\" height=\"19\" />\nand so the proof is complete.<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>To have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859e0c3cda44224a3d8c35d5711fccef2a5d1f8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B + C = 4S\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"159\" height=\"21\" />, we must satisfy \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/8/5e8eca59a434e782a43c6acf9f340cedf8723837.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{A^2 + B^2}{2} = AB,\\]\" width=\"124\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/c/0bcd5541245f359fd933fc673e5b1ee532a1acd6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{B^2 + C^2}{2} = BC,\\]\" width=\"124\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/6/ca6fd2c8605dc5bc6b54fa2b167a01f94deeb7da.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{C^2 + A^2}{2} = CA.\\]\" width=\"122\" height=\"39\" />\nThis is only true when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/d/41d02103d764692ed6ffe64cd1a4755061a0013a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = B = C$\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/0/ec0ce3f851e9d124ca3388a8bbdebb383a00f9dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = b = c$\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" />. Therefore, equality happens when the triangle is equilateral.\n</p><p>~mathboy100\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28duality_principle.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(duality_principle)\">Solution 2 (duality principle)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (duality principle)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We firstly use the duality principle.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/9/82996d7de8e7eda460bae7b59c71a8dc13841f91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=x+y~~b=x+z~~c=y+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"247\" height=\"18\" />\nThe LHS becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/d/23ded5886959b4d707b11141d19adaa0228afcde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+y)^2+(x+z)^2+(y+z)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"233\" height=\"19\" />\nand the RHS becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/3/ee3364b1d5edaa644f5af48aafdcf659c1f54057.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\sqrt{3}\\sqrt{(x+y+z)xyz}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"170\" height=\"35\" /> If we use Heron's formula.\nBy AM-GM <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/a/75a10d5d2540f5680fae9f55a035258a389ac924.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(x+y+z)^3}{27} \\ge xyz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"155\" height=\"41\" />\nMaking this substitution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/3/d33cc80fa8f093e155c5be46d2e5d9da3d7e1ef5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> becomes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f40a77ce3942e4d530ea645a0dbca6bbdfbf1257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(x+y+z)^4\\frac{1}{27}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"137\" height=\"45\" />\nand once we take the square root of the area then our RHS becomes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/b/4cb5d6759e4a9b4fcddad8d10b3bb1810a067041.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3\\sqrt{3}}(x+y+z)^2=\\frac{4}{3}(x+y+z)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"267\" height=\"48\" />\nMultiplying the RHS and the LHS by 3 we get the LHS to be\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/0/3d09ebc5feef1a144fa3d18a53f0ed6d7bd9c347.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3((x+y)^2+(x+z)^2+(y+z)^2)=6(x^2+y^2+z^2+xy+yz+xz).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"533\" height=\"21\" />\nOur RHS becomes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/b/85b7e749b2589947c8bc41c544dff683274cc934.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(x^2+y^2+z^2)+8(xy+yz+xz).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"274\" height=\"21\" />\nSubtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/f/faffa125616367187687ecaa7202d96f84db3a88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(x^2+y^2+z^2)+6(xy+yz+xz)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"269\" height=\"21\" /> we have the LHS equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/3/2f3254e6facbcbf358aa98cb5ca6ad3f292dbabb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2(x^2+y^2+z^2))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"21\" /> and the RHS being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/e/0fe6cfeebb55ab562655d674ab369f612d94a3e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(xy+xz+yz)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />\nIf LHS <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00c3863a5ca53a1be38db8921ae7b5bfbfbe1dc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ge$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> RHS then LHS-RHS<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa9c151a661a687f6e3e9b6e95ff672c231b6ef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" />\nLHS-RHS=<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/9/c890791bb523cfe0e24b64fbdbc3684ab48e84cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(x^2+y^2+z^2)-2(xy+xz+yz)=x^2-2xy+y^2+x^2-2x+z^2+y^2-2yz+z^2=(x-y)^2+(x-z)^2+(y-z)^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"915\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/8/698a6ff46da372338e6b2e38903177d4a56e6407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-y)^2+(x-z)^2+(y-z)^2 \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"269\" height=\"21\" /> by the trivial inequality so therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/f/fef898558ae7541eb052941b83d871b393e690ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2 + c^2 \\ge 4S\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"162\" height=\"19\" /> and we're done.\n</p><p>~PEKKA\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Trigonometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Trigonometry)\">Solution 3 (Trigonometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Trigonometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the angle between edges <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> subtending <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>We notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0decd9758f553dc358bc160ff000b94fdf6d3b52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le(a-b\\cos x)^2=a^2-2ab\\cos x+b^2\\cos^2x\\le a^2-2ab\\cos x+b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"522\" height=\"21\" /> holds for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/0/0e0c2d4b2b0f32a042f89e738346808fbc75a191.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,x\\in\\mathbb R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>If we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/9/529b69f38f906dd7a9f359775dc898689a1cb47e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\theta+30^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/6/bd61c79d331f8e88efc5dc3fa385809638c23ac6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}a^2-2ab\\sin(\\theta+30^\\circ)+b^2&amp;\\geq0\\\\ a^2-2ab(\\sin\\theta\\cos30^\\circ+\\cos\\theta\\sin30^\\circ)+b^2&amp;\\geq0\\\\a^2-ab\\sin\\theta\\sqrt3-ab\\cos\\theta+b^2&amp;\\geq0\\\\a^2-ab\\cos\\theta+b^2&amp;\\geq ab\\sin\\theta\\sqrt3\\\\a^2-ab\\cos\\theta+b^2&amp;\\geq2\\left(\\frac12ab\\sin\\theta\\right)\\sqrt3\\\\a^2-ab\\cos\\theta+b^2&amp;\\geq2T\\sqrt3\\\\2a^2-2ab\\cos\\theta+2b^2&amp;\\geq4T\\sqrt3\\\\a^2+b^2+(a^2-2ab\\cos\\theta+b^2)&amp;\\geq4\\sqrt3\\ T\\\\\\boxed{a^2+b^2+c^2\\geq4\\sqrt3\\ T}\\ \\blacksquare\\end{align*}\" width=\"478\" height=\"286\" />\n</p><p>For equality, it is necessary for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30c9f6d0c626f96446bf84ef225a0ca72b6df296.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2-2ab\\sin x+b^2=0\\implies a=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"268\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/9/d69c5a597013d794032131055c01edcae7906f4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x=\\sin(\\theta+30^\\circ)=1\\implies\\theta=60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"297\" height=\"20\" />, which implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is equilateral.\n</p><p>~ztilB\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Ravi_Substitution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Ravi_Substitution)\">Solution 3 (Ravi Substitution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Ravi Substitution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Again, we use Heron's formula but we also set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/2/cb28159e992d76c897cc82e9c0fb6bd672be7ed7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=y+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bce0c2d7b31d35a82f826070fae7c41f4dab836.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=z+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/1437edba37258088e4e3b3ca44ed1cac2773a142.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/9/7c99b49c0dd1dba95eb6dc6f4167bc9195b93d29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=\\sqrt{xyz(x+y+z)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"173\" height=\"35\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/a/20aadb602e4e5900e3492bb3e18372c5f78d9cc2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 4\\sqrt{3xyz(x+y+z)} &amp;= \\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt{27xyz(x+y+z)} \\\\ &amp;\\le \\frac{4}{3}(x^2+y^2+z^2+2xy+2yz+2zx) \\end{align*}\" width=\"451\" height=\"80\" />\nand if we set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53f1c83051dd99fb9601b2c5f2bc369e126bce4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=xy+yz+zx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/f/fcf81af3aaa3c348150705f1e0a9198ae29b1e85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=x^2+y^2+z^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"20\" /> then it suffices to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/0/010f5e1fdab5c9213be5d281669dd850dc3f2bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B \\le \\frac{2}{3}(A+2B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"164\" height=\"38\" /> which is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/e/68e53e7fcfaac6643ec4dff63ecacbf79d564850.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A\\le B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> and is obviously true. ~alexanderchew2021\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZYOB-KSEF3k&amp;list=PLa8j0YHOYQQJGzkvK2Sm00zrh0aIQnof8&amp;index=4\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZYOB-KSEF3k&amp;list=PLa8j0YHOYQQJGzkvK2Sm00zrh0aIQnof8&amp;index=4</a>\n- AMBRIGGS\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO\" title=\"1961 IMO\">1961 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017163649\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.046 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 389/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 13680/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.958      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.958      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4850:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017163649 and revision id 249980. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}